  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" caput="2" para="true">CAP. II.</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Furcâ Pœnali, &amp; cæsos sub</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="2">eâ ad mortem.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">EA est, <i>quâ item collo impositâ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>circumductì, sed cum verberi-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>bus &amp; pœnæ caussâ.</i> Atque adeò</l>
    <l n="7">mors, plerumque huic consequa:</l>
    <l n="8">sive sub ipsâ Furcâ ad neccm</l>
    <l n="9">cæsis, sive cum eâ in crucem latis.</l>
    <l n="10">Seorsim utrumque explicabo,</l>
    <l n="11">&amp; firmabo. Sub eâ ad mortem</l>
    <l n="12">cæsi: ex Suetonio , <i>qui pœ-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>nam more majorum interpretatur,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>nudi hominis cervicem inseri fur-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>cæ, corpus virgis ad necem cædi.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">Atque idem etiam Victor: <i>Se-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>natus sententiâ constitutum, ut,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>more minorum, collo in furcam con-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>jecto, virgis ad necem caderetur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">Ac reperio exempla etiam in hi-</l>
    <l n="21">storiâ, etsi haud crebra. Li-</l>
    <l n="22">vius * incestum cum Vestale F sic</l>
    <l n="23" type="foot" para="true">1 Neron. cap. xlix. 2 In Nerone.</l>
